            <ArticleTitle>Ergotism unresponsive to multiple therapeutic modalities, including sodium nitroprusside, resulting in limb loss.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>157-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Unlike epidemics in past centuries, patients suffering from peripheral vascular ischemia related to ergotism now rarely lose a limb because of vasodilator therapies. We report a patient with ischemia from ergotamine tartrate who failed to recover with medical therapy, resulting in limb amputation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
